IMPORT prelude

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 1 December 2023 -- LAYER 1: THE NOUNS.  Types only: no rule, no #EVAL.  Every other module of the
-- encoding imports this one.  The membership test for a noun: could a witness of ordinary competence
-- testify to this fact, or does answering it require reading the Act?  Only the first kind is here.
-- The text file is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.

§ `Courts, offices and days`

-- s 3(1) names five State Courts; the other two members are not State Courts.
DECLARE `Court or tribunal` IS ONE OF
    `District Court`
    `Magistrate's Court`
    `Coroner's Court`
    `Small Claims Tribunal`
    `Employment Claims Tribunal`
    `General Division of the High Court`
    `Another court or tribunal`

-- The holders of the offices and posts the Act names.
DECLARE `Holder of an office or post` IS ONE OF
    `District Judge`
    Magistrate
    `Registrar of the State Courts`
    `Deputy registrar of the State Courts`
    `Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
    `Justice of the Peace`
    Bailiff
    `Process server`
    Interpreter
    `Commissioner for oaths`
    `Another officer of a State Court`
    `Supreme Court Judge or Judicial Commissioner`
    `Someone else`

-- s 6A and s 57: the kinds of day on which a State Court sits or the Registry is open.
DECLARE `Kind of day` IS ONE OF
    `Ordinary day`
    Saturday
    Sunday
    `Public holiday`
    `Day in a vacation authorised under section 61`

§ `Section 2 -- the kinds of definition and the table of defined words`

DECLARE `Kind of definition` IS ONE OF
    Means
    Includes
    `Means and includes`
    `Has the meaning given by another law`

-- One entry of the table in s 2: the word, the kind of definition, what the Act names, what it points at, its own words.
DECLARE Definition HAS
    term IS A STRING
    kind IS A `Kind of definition`
    `what the Act names` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `what the Act points at` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the Act's words` IS A STRING

§ `Part 2 -- hearings, private hearings and electronic hearings`

-- s 7(2A): what a State Court may order removed or redacted from a court document.
DECLARE `Material in a court document` IS ONE OF
    `The name, address or photograph of a witness`
    `Evidence or another thing likely to lead to the identification of a witness by a person other than a party`
    `Information that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore`
    `Other material`

-- s 7(3): what a State Court may order that no person is to do.
DECLARE `Act that an order may forbid` IS ONE OF
    `Publish the name, address or photograph of a witness, or evidence likely to lead to the identification of a witness`
    `Do another act likely to lead to the identification of a witness`
    `Publish information that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore`
    `Another act`

-- s 7(5): who the court may permit to be present at a hearing in private.
DECLARE `Individual who might be present` IS ONE OF
    `A journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service`
    `An individual whom the court determines has a sufficient interest in the matter or proceeding`
    `Another individual that the court specifies in the particular case`
    `Anyone else`

-- s 7(6): the matters the court may consider in deciding whether to hear a matter in private.
DECLARE `Matter the court may consider` IS ONE OF
    `Whether the defence of an accused person will be prejudiced by the presence of a member of the public`
    `Whether an accused person or witness has a legitimate interest in privacy that needs to be protected`
    `Whether the object of the matter will be defeated by publicity if heard in open court`
    `Whether an accused person or witness has a legitimate interest in protecting the confidentiality of information that may be disclosed`
    `Whether information that may be disclosed will be prejudicial to the interests of Singapore`
    `Another matter`

-- s 8(1): the means by which a hearing may be conducted.
DECLARE `Means of hearing` IS ONE OF
    `A live video link`
    `A live television link`
    `A live audio link`
    `Another electronic means of communication approved by the Chief Justice`
    `Another electronic means of communication not approved by the Chief Justice`

-- s 8(2): the provisions of other Acts that s 8(1) does not affect.
DECLARE `Provision of another Act` IS ONE OF
    `Section 26A of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016`
    `Section 62A of the Evidence Act 1893`
    `Section 281 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `Another provision`

-- The people and bodies on whom the Act puts a duty, for the regulative rules.
DECLARE `Bearer of a duty` IS ONE OF
    `Any person`
    `A claimant`
    `A judicial officer`
    `A State Court`
    `The Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
    `A District Judge`
    `An officer of a State Court`
    `A bailiff or process server`

-- The acts that the regulative rules regulate.
DECLARE `Act regulated` IS ONE OF
    `contravene an order under section 7(2A) or 7(3)`
    `conduct a part of a hearing through a live audio link only`
    `divide a cause of action for the purpose of bringing two or more actions`
    `take and subscribe the oath of office`
    `give the appellant a reasonable opportunity to show cause`
    `include a person's name in the list of touts before hearing the person`
    `deliver an impounded document out of the custody of the court or allow it to be inspected without an order signed by a judicial officer`
    `accept fees of office, perquisites, emoluments or advantages other than salary and allowances`
    `investigate, try or commit for trial a proceeding in which the judicial officer is a party or personally interested`
    `purchase or bid for property sold in connection with a duty of the officer`
    `execute a writ, summons, warrant, order, notice or other mandatory process`
    `make a return of the process and the manner of its execution to the court from which it issued`
    `arrest and receive the persons and property committed to the custody of the State Courts`
    `sign the process and bear the seal of the court`

§ `Part 3 -- appointments, powers and duties`

-- s 17(2): before whom the oath may be taken and subscribed.
DECLARE `Person administering an oath` IS ONE OF
    `The Presiding Judge of the State Courts`
    `The Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts`
    `A Supreme Court Judge or a Judicial Commissioner`
    `Someone else`

-- s 15(1): the duties of bailiffs and process servers.
DECLARE `Duty of a bailiff or process server` IS ONE OF
    `Execute the writs, summonses, warrants, orders, notices and other mandatory processes of the State Courts given to them`
    `Make a return of the same, with the manner of the execution, to the court from which the process issued`
    `Arrest and receive the persons and property committed to the custody of the State Courts`
    `Some other duty`

-- The Schedule: one form of oath.
DECLARE `Oath form` HAS
    `item of the Schedule` IS A NUMBER
    `taken by` IS A STRING
    words IS A STRING


§ `Part 4 -- the civil action and the powers of a court in it`

-- One civil action, the natural unit of Part 4: the facts a claimant or defendant could state about it.
-- The two steps that follow the start of an action (the claimant's abandonment of the excess, s 22, and the parties' signed agreement, s 23) are fields too.
DECLARE `Civil action` HAS
    `the action is in personam` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant was served in Singapore in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant was served outside Singapore in the circumstances authorised by and in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the court asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim includes a claim for a sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount claimed in dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `the value in dollars of the subject matter of any remedy or relief sought` IS A NUMBER
    `the action is in passing off` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action is within a supervisory or revisionary jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the action is for judicial review of an act or decision, including a Mandatory Order, a Prohibiting Order, a Quashing Order or an Order for Review of Detention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `jurisdiction over the action is vested exclusively in the General Division of the High Court, a Family Court, a Youth Court, another State Court or a tribunal by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `jurisdiction over the action is expressly excluded by written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `section 28A of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969, or an order under its subsection (1), affects the action` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant has abandoned the excess amount or the remedy or relief` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parties agreed, by a memorandum signed by them or their solicitors, that the court is to have jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 25: the facts about an action for the recovery of immovable property.
DECLARE `Recovery of immovable property` HAS
    `it is an action for the recovery of immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the annual value of the property appearing in the Valuation List` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the annual rent payable by the tenant` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the monthly rent payable by the tenant` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the last transacted price of the property` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

-- s 26: the proceedings in equity that a District Court may hear (paragraphs (a) and (e) are deleted).
DECLARE `Kind of equity proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `Execution of a trust, or a declaration that a trust subsists`
    `Foreclosure or redemption of a mortgage, or enforcement of a charge or lien`
    `Specific performance, or rectification, delivery up or cancellation, of an agreement for the sale, purchase or lease of property`
    `Dissolution or winding up of a partnership`
    `Relief against fraud or mistake`
    `Another kind of proceeding`

-- s 26: one equity proceeding and the amount or value that the paragraph measures against the District Court limit.
DECLARE `Equity proceeding` HAS
    kind IS A `Kind of equity proceeding`
    `the amount or value that the paragraph measures` IS A NUMBER
    `the partnership is a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 29(1): one claim for relief by way of interpleader.
DECLARE `Interpleader claim` HAS
    `a bailiff of a District Court is charged with the execution of a writ or order of the Court and a person other than the person against whom it was issued claims the money or movable property taken or intended to be taken, or its proceeds or value` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person seeking relief is under liability for a debt, money or other movable property and has been or expects to be sued by 2 or more parties making adverse claims to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount or value of that debt, money or movable property` IS A NUMBER

-- ss 31 and 52(1B): the powers of a court in an action within its jurisdiction.
DECLARE `Power of a court in a civil action` IS ONE OF
    `Grant any relief, redress or remedy, or combination of remedies, absolute or conditional`
    `Give effect to every ground of defence or counterclaim, equitable or legal`
    `Grant an injunction`
    `Make a binding declaration of rights`
    `Order the medical examination of a party`
    `Make an order or exercise an authority which a Judge in chambers in the General Division of the High Court could make or exercise`
    `Exercise a power that section 43 or 49A gives a District Court`
    `Exercise a power that section 12 of the Civil Law Act 1909 gives a District Court`
    `Another power`

-- s 48(2): when the agreement not to appeal was made.
DECLARE `When an agreement was made` IS ONE OF
    `Before the decision was made`
    `After the decision was made`
    `At another time`

-- ss 54E(2) and 54F(2): the three orders the court may make on a counterclaim that is beyond the limit.
DECLARE `Order on a counterclaim beyond the limit` IS ONE OF
    `Transfer the whole proceedings to the higher court`
    `Try the whole proceedings in the lower court`
    `Transfer the counterclaim to the higher court and try the claim and defence in the lower court`
    `Another order`
